+The Action! compiler now emits native scalar/direct/indirect calls and supplies
+an independently assembled context bridge. Its slice 7 qualification uses the
+corrected production CPU timing: REP/SEP commit status at the final cycle and
+RTI IRQ sampling sees the status byte on its pull cycle. The old cycle-reference
+mode is test-only; see the core notice for the separated evidence.
 
-No scheduler, allocator, message system or general Atari 65816 machine model
